{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-self-duality","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:categorical-self-duality","kind":"proof","title":"Proof of Categorical self-duality","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-self-duality"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.categorical_self_duality","text":"categorical-self-duality-proof.md","leanSource":"categorical-self-duality-proof.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:categorical-self-duality\"></a><p>By the Bogomolny decomposition in the dagger category,</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\int_A(F_\\nabla^* \\cdot F_\\nabla)\n  =  2\\int_A({F_\\nabla^-}^* \\cdot F_\\nabla^-)\n        + \\int_A(F_\\nabla \\wedge_q F_\\nabla),</code></pre>\n<p>where the second term is topological (determined by the class\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[F_\\nabla] \\in \\Omega^2(A)/\\mathrm{exact}</code>).  Minimising\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S[\\nabla]</code> forces <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F_\\nabla^- = 0</code>, which is exactly the\nself-duality condition.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-self-duality-proof.md","heading":"Proof","page":"b/prf-categorical-self-duality","qa":{"counts":{"pass":64,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":8,"unknown":0,"stale":60},"milnor":{"total":1,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.categorical_self_duality","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-self-duality-proof.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
